{{ ref: 6fa0c0d3-617d-410b-99a6-2440f4c5818f }}
```rust
pub struct Finding {
  pub kind: FindingKind,      // cycle | polarity | capacity | visibility
  pub severity: Severity,     // violation | borderline
  pub location: Vec<NodeRef>, // offending symbols / files / containers
  pub detail: String,         // human narration incl. break suggestions
}
```
--{ ref: 6fa0c0d3-617d-410b-99a6-2440f4c5818f }--

{{ ref: 41e55228-2706-40a1-ad72-a82fc3b659f1 }}
- **Behaviour**: Analysis always exits `0` when it completes — violations are findings, not failures; exit `2` is reserved for `--fail-on` matches. `borderline` findings (within ±10% of a cap) never gate, absorbing formatter churn. Cycle findings embed the shatter phase's break suggestions with their `exact` flag, so the violation table doubles as a fix list.
--{ ref: 41e55228-2706-40a1-ad72-a82fc3b659f1 }--
{{ ref: 92b81bde-a8c9-41f4-8f1d-1f9b8328c9bf }}
- **Compatibility**: First release. New finding kinds may be added in minor versions; an unrecognized class in `--fail-on` raises `ConfigInvalid`, so CI configurations fail loudly rather than silently not gating.
--{ ref: 92b81bde-a8c9-41f4-8f1d-1f9b8328c9bf }--